-- title:
--   Integral logarithmic covector of a formal-group logarithm
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$ and $c^{p}-c$ lies in the ideal $(p)$ for every $c\in\mathcal{O}$. Let $d\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $\varphi\in\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ be a multivariate power series subject to the integrality condition that for every coordinate $j$ and every multi-index $m\in\mathbb{N}^{d}$ the element $(m_j+1)\cdot\operatorname{coeff}_{m+e_j}(\varphi)$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^{|m|}$, where $|m|$ denotes the total degree; equivalently, $M_j\,\operatorname{coeff}_M(\varphi)\in p^{|M|-1}\mathcal{O}$ for all $M\neq 0$. Fix $N\in\mathbb{N}$ and a family $c_m\in\mathcal{O}$ indexed by multi-indices $m$ such that: if $|m|\le N$ then $c_m=p^{\,N-|m|}\operatorname{coeff}_m(\varphi)$; and if $|m|>N$ then either $c_m\cdot p^{\,|m|-N}=\operatorname{coeff}_m(\varphi)$, or $c_m=0$ and $p^{\,|m|-N}$ does not divide $\operatorname{coeff}_m(\varphi)$. Then there exists a Witt vector $\ell\in W(\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]])$ whose ghost components realise the rescaled coefficient families: for every $n<N$ and every multi-index $m'$, the coefficient of $X^{m'}$ in the $n$-th ghost component of $\ell$ equals $c_{p^{\,N-1-n}m'}$ (truncated subtraction in the exponent).
--
--   This is the integrality statement underlying Fontaine's finite-level logarithmic covector: the rescaled coefficient series $\gamma_n$ attached to a logarithm-type power series form the ghost sequence of an actual Witt vector over $\mathcal{O}[[X]]$, the key point being Dwork-style congruences supplied by the hypotheses on $\varphi$ and on $p$-power divisibility. It is obtained from a criterion for prescribing finitely many ghost components in terms of a lift of Frobenius together with the congruence $\operatorname{expand}_p(f)\equiv f^{p}\pmod p$ on power series, and it feeds the deformation-theoretic lemmas that place truncated Witt vectors in the Fontaine kernel of a multivariate formal group.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_wittVector_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector.lean

